A||||5||Master_Sushi||Windshield Wiper Park||||4||
Z||000000||Master_Sushi||02-02-2001||04:15 PM||||I have a problum with my wipers. They work fine, except they dont go down to the bottom of the windshield when I turn them off. They jsut stop whereever they happen to be. Ive jsut taken apart my wipers and took off the motor but I cant find the park sensor on it (if i'm looking in the right spot). The motor is completely sealed. I was reading up on some older posts about it. What am I missing here?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>edit- Im also assuming I just have to clean the sensor up and greese it. Because if I turn the wipers off in the middle of the windshield, then shake them a bit they will *sometimes* move down to the right spot. I also jsut have the plain HI-LOW-OFF wipers.<P>Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 02-02-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Phaeton||02-02-2001||11:10 PM||||The park switch should be located somewhere on the output end of the gears near the crank arm's shaft.  It works off a cam that opens a contact set when the arm is in the full down position.  It's cold out, but if it cannot be found I will brave the elements and eyeball the one on my 88GT for all the details.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||02-03-2001||09:28 AM||||Ok, I opened up my wiper motor today. I think I found the switch. I cleaned it up by sanding it, and making sure it made contact. But still dosent work. So I wired it up and manualy activated the switch with a screwdriver. It just blew a fuse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> . Would it fix the problum if I just bought a whole new wiper motor at autozone? They are like $50 and im getting sick of just dicking around with this old broken one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||02-03-2001||10:02 AM||||My fathers wipers stopped parking about five years ago.  While the car was in for service for something else he had the tech check it out.  The response was that it needed a new wiper motor since its all one unit.  He decided to not have it replaced and just lived with the wipers and turn them off when they are at the bottom.  However, we did get one at a junk yard recently for our rebuilding project of the car so they should be working good soon!  It sounds like you may need a new motor to remedy the problem.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||02-03-2001||06:14 PM||||check  with junkyard wiper motor common used in many cars by G M . cost 20-25 at most. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-03-2001||06:29 PM||||I plan on keeping my car for a lonngggggg time so if i have problems like that I just replace it with new, so I dont have to do it again a couple of years down the road.||||reg||1
